      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "This is a reevaluation of registered nurse (RN) supply and demand from 2016 to 2030 using a previously published work forecast model and grading methodology with more recent workforce data. There will be a shortage of 154 018 RNs by 2020 and 510 394 RNs by 2030; the South and West regions will have higher shortage ratios than Northeast and Midwest regions. This reflects a nearly 50% overall improvement when compared with the authors' prior study, and the low-performing states have improved from 18 \"D\" and 12 \"F\" grades as published earlier to 13 \"D\" and 1 \"F\" in this study. Although progress has been made, efforts to foster the pipelines for improving the nursing workforce need to be continued."},
